<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;GWENNO SAUNDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gwenno Saunders is a Welsh singer-songwriter known for her enchanting vocals and eclectic style, fascinated by the rich tapestry of Cornish identity and the natural world."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILADELPHIA MUSIC VENUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Philadelphia music venue is an iconic stage where Gwenno performed, leaving the crowd buzzing with energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIFF BOOKSTORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardiff bookstore is where Gwenno found an old, treasured volume on ornithology that captivated her."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMY OF NATURAL SCIENCES OF DREXEL UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University is an institution where Gwenno discussed a potential collaboration with Dr. Rachel Kim."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. RACHEL KIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Rachel Kim is the director of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University, inviting Gwenno to discuss a project that would weave together music, science, and conservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORNITHOLOGY BOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ornithology book is a treasured volume on birds in flight and their habitats, which Gwenno often found herself lost in."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GORSEDH KERNOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gorsedh Kernow is a centuries-old institution dedicated to the preservation and promotion of Cornish language, literature, and culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D.M. THOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"D.M. Thomas is a Cornish poet whose writing influenced Gwenno's lyrical style."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORNWALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cornwall is the region where Gwenno's family relocated, and where she discovered the works of D.M. Thomas and forged a connection with the Cornish cultural heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELSH LANGUAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Welsh language is a tradition instilled in Gwenno by her parents, and a part of her cultural identity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Y DYDD OLAF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Y Dydd Olaf is Gwenno's debut solo album, released in 2015, featuring songs in both Welsh and Cornish, marking a turning point in her career."&lt;SEP&gt;"Y Dydd Olaf is the title of Gwenno's debut solo album, released in 2015, which gained critical acclaim and commercial success."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIFF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardiff is the city where Gwenno was born and where her parents instilled in her a deep love for Welsh language and folk music."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL WORLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The natural world is a source of inspiration for Gwenno, with its rhythms and melodies reflecting in her music."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TALLEST DINOSAUR SKELETONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tallest dinosaur skeletons are on display at the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University, showcasing the institution's historical collections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRIDESCENT BUTTERFLY SPECIMENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iridescent butterfly specimens are on display at the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University, highlighting the institution's scientific collections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANCIENT, FOSSILIZED TREES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient, fossilized trees are on display at the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University, representing the institution's paleontological collections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATELY FAÇADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The stately façade of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University is a symbol of the institution's historical significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HALLOWED HALLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The hallowed halls of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Drexel University are a place of reverence and discovery."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUSTY CARDIFF BOOKSTORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The dusty Cardiff bookstore is where Gwenno found the ornithology book that captivated her."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TATTOO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gwenno has a tattoo that represents her connection to the natural world and her cultural heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TATTOO OF A BIRD IN FLIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tattoo of a bird in flight on Gwenno's arm symbolizes her deep connection to the natural world and her artistic expression."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TATTOO OF A WELSH DRAGON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tattoo of a Welsh dragon on Gwenno's arm represents her cultural identity and heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAUNDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saunders is mentioned as the subject of the text, though her full name is not provided."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GWENNO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gwenno is a musician who released her debut solo album in 2015 and is known for her work in promoting Celtic languages and cultures."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2015&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2015 is the year in which Gwenno released her debut solo album, marking a significant milestone in her career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELSH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Welsh is one of the languages used in Gwenno's debut album, highlighting her cultural contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORNISH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cornish is another language used in Gwenno's debut album, further emphasizing her dedication to Celtic cultures."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELTIC LANGUAGES AND CULTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Celtic languages and cultures are the focus of Gwenno's work, particularly through her album Y Dydd Olaf."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRITICAL ACCLAIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical acclaim refers to the positive reception of Gwenno's debut album Y Dydd Olaf."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL SUCCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Commercial success refers to the financial and market success of Gwenno's debut album Y Dydd Olaf."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBUT SOLO ALBUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debut solo album is the specific event of Gwenno releasing her first solo album, Y Dydd Olaf."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0162</data>
    </node>
